V3-4 test batch (Oracle-B; verified and re-reported by Oracle against HEAD
2c520aa, 2026-09-29). NOT applied to test/ yet — the flip lands together with
V3-4 (TSK-028, .nanojira/ + migration).

tools/v34-batch/nj-v34-batch-transform.py   the generator: python3 nj-v34-batch-transform.py <tree root>
                                            edits <root>/test in place; asserts every special-case anchor,
                                            so it fails loudly instead of mis-editing.
tools/v34-batch/nj-v34-batch.patch          a git diff captured against 6b75df0 (before the V3-3 batch and
                                            everything since). STALE relative to current HEAD — test/ has
                                            moved (the V3-3 batch, T1-T3, v3-2-regressions.js, coverage
                                            gaps, ac-25/ac-26). Kept for reference only; do not `git apply`
                                            it. Regenerate with `git diff` after running the script, if a
                                            patch form is wanted again.

Verification (2026-09-29, Oracle): ran the script in a throwaway worktree at
HEAD 2c520aa. It applied cleanly — every `must()` anchor matched, zero
assertion failures, every edited file's syntax checks with `node --check`.
A full-tree grep afterward confirms no `.js` file outside the two
intentional exceptions (`ac/ac-24-legacy-migration.js`,
`edge/coverage-v3-gaps.js`) still names a v2 bookkeeping path as a literal —
the three remaining hits are the deliberate ones: the history note in
ac-21's header comment, and ac-01's new "no v2 file exists" assertion, which
names `.nanojira.json`/`.ids` on purpose to check their ABSENCE. No script
changes were needed; this batch was already correct for the current tree.

What it does:
- test/lib/harness.js: new exports CONFIG_REL='.nanojira/config.json', IDS_REL='.nanojira/ids',
  INDEX_REL='.nanojira/index.json', GITIGNORE; mkBacklog() builds the v3 layout.
- every suite that names a bookkeeping path: '.nanojira.json' -> H.CONFIG_REL, '.ids' -> H.IDS_REL,
  v2 .gitignore -> H.GITIGNORE, index skip -> r === H.INDEX_REL; prose .nanojira.json/.ids//.nanojira-index.json
  -> v3 names. 31 files, listed below.
- ac-22/ac-23: local CONFIG_REL/IDS_REL now = H.*; staging comments rewritten to say "since V3-4" instead
  of "V3-4 flips them".
- ac-01: checks .nanojira/, the v3 config path, the .gitignore pair, ".nanojira/ids/ never ignored"
  (also not via ignoring the whole .nanojira/ folder), no v2 files at the top level, and the full § 5
  layout block (DECISIONS 92 Q1).
- fault/det-id-retry.js: the EEXIST shim's tombstone-path regex matches .nanojira/ids/.
- ac-21: one history comment updated (says "since V3-4" instead of describing a future move); its
  fixtures are hand-built by H.mkBacklog() regardless, so no functional change.
- ac-24-legacy-migration.js and edge/coverage-v3-gaps.js are excluded on purpose: their v2 paths are
  the legacy layout under test, not staging.
- harness's STATUS_CONFIG_REL (the V3-3 STATUS.md renderer, Oracle's batch) flips to
  '.nanojira/config.json' too, via the same run.

