Deliberately untouched: ac/ac-24-legacy-migration.js, edge/coverage-v3-gaps.js
(v2 paths spelled out on purpose), and every other suite that never names a
bookkeeping path directly (ac-25-note-author.js, a future ac-27 for `nj claim` when it lands,
edge/hardening-v3-1.js, edge/hardening-njrc-foreign-link.js — these reach
config/tombstones only through H.mkBacklog()/H.* and need no edit).

Caveat, inherent and not a bug: the flipped tree, run against any nj that
does not yet implement V3-4, will crash or fail hard wherever a fixture
writes bookkeeping files directly (bypassing nj) at the new paths — e.g.
edge/v3-2-regressions.js's R6 fixture writes tombstones straight to
H.IDS_REL after `nj init`, and a pre-V3-4 `nj init` only ever creates the v2
`.ids/`. That is expected: this batch is meant to be applied together with
a V3-4-capable `nj`, not run against today's build. Do not read a crash from
that combination as a script defect.

How to apply when V3-4 lands:
  python3 tools/v34-batch/nj-v34-batch-transform.py <path to the working tree>
(pass the repo root, not test/ — the script joins 'test' itself). Then run
the oracle against the new dist/nj and fix whatever the real V3-4 changes
call for beyond this mechanical rename.
